Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:30:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 174/174] docs: the film grain ships as G0 + G1; plates and EXR
 metadata are parked, and the docs say so

The user froze the feature on 2026-09-11: the basic film grain is good enough, so G0 (the
skeleton and the white-Gaussian cell generator) plus G1 (the digital sensor model) are what
ships, and G2 (grain plates) and G3 (EXR metadata and measurement tools) wait for a concrete
camera-emulation need. The specification was still written as though all four stages were coming,
which meant three documents described a plate pipeline and an export block that do not exist.

FilmGrainSpec.md
- Status line states what shipped, and gives each parked stage a one-line reason.
- 3.3 (film plates) marked PARKED, not implemented, with a note that the Film family uses the
  3.5 white-Gaussian cell generator instead and that the offline synthesis tool exists untracked
  at ReC-Sandbox/tools/grain-plates/.
- 3.5 marked as the shipped Film generator rather than a placeholder "before plates exist".
- 7 (export) marked PARKED: no rec.grain.* metadata is written and no grain-apply tool exists.
- 9 stage list carries SHIPPED / PARKED per stage.

README.md
- The Film family is described for what it is: a procedural per-cell Gaussian on a grid in film
  millimetres, shaped by a response curve, shipping with no assets at all.
- The preset table's DSNU column follows the residuals of the previous commit
  (0.15 / 0.45 / 0.06 e-), and the paragraph under it explains why DSNU is quoted post-calibration
  while row, column and PRNU are not.

docs/ConsoleReference.md
- Verified the three cvars against RendererCVars.cpp and the Grain_User_* list against the
  registrations in PostProcess.cpp; both already matched.
- The uploaded response LUT is now described as parked with G2 rather than "arriving in G2", and
  the two texture-id params are marked as always 0 for the same reason.

